x already upgrades older ledgers in x: schema 3 rewrites scalar notes, schema 4 sets the version, and the other verbs refuse both with a message that names x (x in x).

# qctl openspec/changes/horizon-reason/proposal.md
A horizon row carries two fields that keep it off the queue.
x names what would end the wait, and x says why the row waits: x, x, or x.
x names a category without saying what varies, which is the "kind as a noun" pattern the prose rules reject.
A reader has to learn from the docs that the field is the reason the row is not startable.

