# rgbctl docs/hardware-test-2026-11-08.md
Whether per-LED colours stay on the devices after the sender stops.

# rgbctl docs/protocol.md
SignalRGB and OpenRGB name the records in the same order: JARGB 1 to 3, JAF, JPIPE 1 to 5, JRGB 1 and 2, onboard 1 to 6, and a last record for all zones ("SelectAll").
Sources: SignalRGB's x (plugin, line 898), and the comments of OpenRGB's x (x, line 178).
MSI's x puts JRGB1 at area 9, which agrees (MB800 notes, zone mapping).

# rgbctl docs/protocol.md
Observed: ColorRing is a chase along the chain.
The colours run through the devices one after another in header order, JARGB_V2_1, V2_2, V2_3, and each device starts just before the previous one finishes.
At brightness 5 and medium speed it looked like many colours with the devices out of sync, each light dark about half the time; at brightness 1 and slow speed (style x) the chase was plain to see.

